{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.62,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "extra_component",
      "components": ["J11"],
      "pins": ["J11.1", "J11.2"],
      "nets": ["GND", "/Microcontroller/NET0001"],
      "observed": "J11 is a two-pin screw terminal. Pin 1 is connected to GND and pin 2 is connected to /Microcontroller/NET0001, the same net as ESP32 GPIO1 (U9 pin 13) and the TPS1H200 high-side switch input/diagnostic-enable pins (U11 pins 1 and 2).",
      "expected": "The specification describes the heater control net as being driven by the ESP32 GPIO1 into the smart high-side switch, with no user-accessible screw terminal on that control net. A 3.3 V logic/control net should not be brought out to a two-terminal connector adjacent to GND without protection, current limiting, or a documented interface role.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"J11\")\n      (value \"Screw_Terminal_01x02\")"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"4\") (name \"/Microcontroller/NET0001\") ... (node (ref \"J11\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"Pin_2\") (pintype \"passive\")) ... (node (ref \"U9\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"GPIO1/ADC1_CH1/XTAL_32K_N\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"8\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"J11\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"Pin_1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "IN/DIAG_EN (pins 1/2) are both driven from ESP32 GPIO1 (net `/Microcontroller/HEATER`), `OUT` (pin 7) feeds the heater connector `J6` pin 2"}
      ],
      "impact": "If the J11 terminal is jumpered or wired, GPIO1 can be pulled toward ground or otherwise loaded, fighting the MCU output and potentially disabling the heater or damaging the GPIO. This is an undocumented external connection on the heater-control signal.",
      "confidence": 0.62
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The connectivity otherwise matches the specified CF-Chef architecture, but J11 is an extra screw terminal tied directly to the heater-control GPIO/high-side-switch input net, which is not part of the intended design and can externally short or load that control signal."
}

